# Architecture

## This repo owns

- REST on the `api` Cloud Function
- Live Gemini session and transcript persistence
- Interview create, score, XP, streak, skills, and achievement updates on complete
- `GET /v2/admin/users` for the superAdmin user list

## This repo does not own

- Candidate or admin screens
- A Super Admin REST API for a screen that already reads Firestore from superAdmin
- Re-enabling callables commented out in `functions/src/index.ts` (`onInterviewComplete` and the other unused exports). Active exports are `api`, `onUserDeleted`, `checkExpiredSubscriptions`, `computeCareerProgress`, and `resetWeeklyDeltas`.

## How code is organized

This is not one MVC tree. Follow the module you are editing.

- V2 HTTP: `functions/src/modules/v2/*.routes.ts` validates with Zod, calls a service, responds with `sendSuccess` / `sendCreated`.
- Auth, coding, and companies use a controller in front of the service. Match that module if you extend it.
- Gemini goes through `functions/src/library/gemini-client.ts`.
- Interview writes go through `functions/src/services/interview.service.ts` or `functions/src/modules/v2/v2-live-interview.persistence.ts`.
- Firestore access uses `firebase-admin` and `functions/src/utils/firestore-refs.ts`.

## Side effects

Changing start config, the system prompt, a socket `type`, `decideAiTurn`, persistence, or `completeInterview` affects the IV-frontend setup, live page, and report. Keep those clients working. Keep v1 (`functions/src/modules/interview`, `functions/src/modules/live-interview`) beside v2. Do not merge them in an unrelated change.
